# THE LAN BOX (step L2 of work/plans/join-template-commit-reveal.md, PL2-8): the
# user's `ethereum-lan-node`, geth in dev mode, chain 19216801, a faucet that
# speaks the framework's faucet API. `pnpm build lan` once `pnpm
# contracts:deploy lan` has written `contracts/deployments/lan`.
#
# EVERY URL IS SAME-HOST (`//:8545` is "the host this page came from, port
# 8545", resolved in the browser: web/src/lib/core/env/same-host.ts), so one
# build works on the box's hotspot address, on a venue's network and by its
# mDNS name. The box serves over plain http, which is not a secure context.
PUBLIC_NODE_URL="//:8545"
PUBLIC_CHAIN_INFO_NODE_URL="//:8545"
# Nobody on a LAN has a wallet for this chain: a burner per browser, funded by
# the box's faucet (1 ETH a claim, no captcha).
PUBLIC_USE_BURNER_WALLET=$PUBLIC_NODE_URL
PUBLIC_FAUCET_API="//:34010"
PUBLIC_FAUCET_LINK="//:34010"
# No internet on the box: no published snapshot (a LAN chain is new, the
# indexer folds it from its first block), no ENS, no reveal scheduler.
PUBLIC_SNAPSHOT_URI=
PUBLIC_ENS_NODE_URL=
PUBLIC_FUZD_URI=
